{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019KzNyNNqzA4PA3C7W8ANFg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/internal.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! quic-core's grand internal header.  Anything that is not\n4\t//! part of the published `quic.h` API but is shared between\n5\t//! `.c` files of the core library lives here: connection /\n6\t//! path / stream / packet structures, frame and packet-type\n7\t//! enums, the giant `Quic` and `Connection`\n8\t//! structures that pin the rest of the library together, and\n9\t//! the long internal-only function surface (~200 functions).\n10\t//!\n11\t//! Phase 4: all function bodies have been filled in.\n12\t//!\n13\t//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n14\t//!\n15\t//! * Single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields collapse to\n16\t//!   `bool` per field (the \"ordinary integer field with\n17\t//!   mask/shift accessors\" rule, simplified for the trivial\n18\t//!   1-bit case where `bool` is clearer than `u32` + masks).\n19\t//! * Phase 1B replaced the C intrusive linked-list / splay /\n20\t//!   hash linkage with arena tokens\n21\t//!   ([`crate::arena::Token`], [`crate::splay::SplayToken`],\n22\t//!   [`crate::hash::HashToken`]).  Every per-collection\n23\t//!   membership is `Option<Token>` on the parent struct; the\n24\t//!   container holds the slot storage.  Zero raw pointers, no\n25\t//!   `unsafe`.\n26\t//! * The C `void* tls_master_ctx`, `void* aead_*`,\n27\t//!   `void* pn_enc/dec`, etc. were external-library handles\n28\t//!   ((picotls, OpenSSL).  Phase 2 replaced them with the\n29\t//!   trait family in [`crate::tls`] (`Session`, `PacketKey`,\n30\t//!   `HeaderKey`, …); backends supply implementations.\n31\t//! * `FILE* F_log` / `FILE* f_binlog` became\n32\t//!   `Option<std::fs::File>` in Phase 1B.\n33\t//! * `struct sockaddr_storage` fields fold into\n34\t//!   [`core::net::SocketAddr`].  Fields that the C code zeros out\n35\t//!   to mean \"address absent\" become `Option<SocketAddr>`.\n36\t//! * `Quic`, `Connection`, `Path` were\n37\t//!   forward-declared as opaque handles in\n38\t//!   [`crate`] (the public header).  Their\n39\t//!   real bodies live here; the public module re-exports the\n40\t//!   names so existing `use` paths in other modules keep\n41\t//!   working.\n42\t//! * Function pointer typedefs (`autoqlog_fn`,\n43\t//!   `performance_log_fn`, the spin-bit pair, the\n44\t//!   memlog hook on a connection, `mask_fns_t`) collapse to\n45\t//!   traits per the project rule.  When two function pointers\n46\t//!   are always installed together (`SpinbitDef`,\n47\t//!   `mask_fns_t`) they share one trait.\n48\t//! * Conditional fields gated by `BBRExperiment` and\n49\t//!   `WITH_THREAD_CHECK` are dropped — they are not\n50\t//!   part of the v1 target build.\n51\t//! * The `PARSE_*`/`IS_*_STREAM_ID(_*)` macros that the C\n52\t//!   header inlines as preprocessor macros are translated to\n53\t//!   `pub const fn` helpers.\n54\t\n55\tuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, VecDeque};\n56\tuse std::fs::File;\n57\tuse std::io::{Read, Write};\n58\tuse std::path::PathBuf;\n59\t\n60\tuse core::any::Any;\n61\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n62\t\n63\tuse crate::arena::{Arena, Token};\n64\tuse crate::hash::{HashTable, HashToken};\n65\tuse crate::splay::{SplayToken, SplayTree};\n66\tuse crate::{Duration, Instant};\n67\t\n68\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` connection arena.\n69\t///\n70\t/// Phase 4 plan: every C `*mut picoquic_cnx_t` becomes a\n71\t/// [`ConnectionToken`].  Following it requires `quic.connections.get(tok)`\n72\t/// — one indirection through the arena, plus a generation check.\n73\t/// Stable across operations on other connections.\n74\tpub type ConnectionToken = Token<Connection>;\n75\t\n76\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` registered-token replay-protection arena.\n77\tpub type RegisteredTokenToken = Token<RegisteredToken>;\n78\t\n79\t/// Token into the per-`Quic` issued-tickets arena (server-side replay state).\n80\tpub type IssuedTicketToken = Token<IssuedTicket>;\n81\t\n82\t/// Token into the per-`Connection` (or per-`StreamHead`) stream-related\n83\t/// arenas.  Phase 4 may further split these into per-collection types.\n84\tpub type StreamToken = Token<StreamHead>;\n85\tpub type StreamDataToken = Token<StreamDataNode>;\n86\tpub type PacketToken = Token<Packet>;\n87\tpub type SackItemToken = Token<SackItem>;\n88\tpub type LocalConnectionIdToken = Token<LocalConnectionId>;\n89\tpub type PathToken = Token<Path>;\n90\tuse crate::logger::LoggerRef;\n91\tuse crate::{\n92\t    AlpnSelect, CongestionAlgorithm, ConnectionId, ConnectionIdCallback, Fuzz, LossbitVersion,\n93\t    PacketContext, PathStatus, PmtudPolicy, RESET_SECRET_SIZE, SpinbitVersion, State,\n94\t    StreamDataCallback, StreamDirectReceive, TransportParameters,\n95\t};\n96\t\n97\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n98\t// Tunable constants (the `#define`s at the top of the C header).\n99\t\n100\tpub const MAX_PACKET_SIZE: usize = 1536;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e85c7bed-bd05-4049-931b-16153c644e2c","uuid":"7fdb0b0b-c44c-4ed9-b317-18d357c6bd24","timestamp":"2026-05-07T09:02:06.884Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/internal.rs","content":"//! Translation of `quic/internal.h`.\n//!\n//! quic-core's grand internal header.  Anything that is not\n//! part of the published `quic.h` API but is shared between\n//! `.c` files of the core library lives here: connection /\n//! path / stream / packet structures, frame and packet-type\n//! enums, the giant `Quic` and `Connection`\n//! structures that pin the rest of the library together, and\n//! the long internal-only function surface (~200 functions).\n//!\n//! Phase 4: all function bodies have been filled in.\n//!\n//! Translation policy notes for this module:\n//!\n//! * Single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields collapse to\n//!   `bool` per field (the \"ordina